          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Bousfield localization of spectra
            refers generally to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localizations
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} stable (∞,1)-category of spectra
            (hence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories+of+spectra"} model categories of spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            which become
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences"} equivalences
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product
            with a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            represents a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology+theory"} generalized homology theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+localization"} homology localization
          %p
            More specifically, if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} stable (∞,1)-category of spectra
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presented
            by a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+model+category"}> stable
            )
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} ∞-categorical localization
            can be presented by the operation of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of model categories
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Bousfield79"} Bousfield 79
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
          %p
            Specifically, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Spec
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in Spec
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %em
              Bousfield localization at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            of another
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi E
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \longrightarrow L_E X
          %p
            to the
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+spectrum"} local spectrum
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi E
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_E X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            any
            = succeed "-acyclic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi E
                    %mo ≃
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \wedge E \simeq 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi E
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \longrightarrow L_E X
            is null-homotopic (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero morphism
            in the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} stable (∞,1)-category of spectra
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie10"} Lurie 10, Example 4
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = M \mathbb{Z}_p
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+spectrum"} Moore spectrum
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi p
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_p \coloneqq \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "-localization" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-completion"} p-completion
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie10"} Lurie 10, Examples 7 and 8
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            We write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spectra)
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in Ho(Spectra)
            two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,Y] \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            for its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
